      <h2>7. Contact by email</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to me at <a href="mailto:hello@brewmind.app">hello@brewmind.app</a>,
        for instance to register for the beta, I process your email address and the content of
        your message in order to answer it. Your message is stored with my email provider. I
        delete the correspondence as soon as it is no longer needed and no statutory retention
        obligation stands in the way.
      </p>
      <p>
        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR insofar as it concerns participation in the beta,
        otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in answering requests).
      </p>

      <h2>8. This website</h2>
      <h3>Hosting</h3>
      <p>
        This website is delivered via <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub Inc.,
        88 Colin P Kelly Jr St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA, a company of Microsoft
        Corporation). When it is accessed, your browser transmits technically necessary data,
        which GitHub processes in server log files:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address of the requesting computer</li>
        <li>Date and time of the request</li>
        <li>Address of the page accessed (URL)</li>
        <li>Referrer URL (page visited previously)</li>
        <li>Browser and operating system used</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; the legitimate interest lies in the technically
        error-free delivery and the security of the website. GitHub Inc. is certified under the
        EU-US Data Privacy Framework. More in
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Pages that hand over to the app</h3>
      <p>
        The page brewmind.app/auth/apple is the return route of „Mit Apple anmelden“ on Android.
        After sign-in, Apple redirects your browser there and appends the response to the
        address, namely in the part after the hash sign, which the browser does not send to the
        server. The page passes the response on to the app, stores nothing and then removes the
        response from the address bar. The address accessed may remain in your browser's
        history.
      </p>
      <p>
        The page brewmind.app/e opens an invitation to a household in the app. Here too, the
        code is after the hash sign and does not reach the server.
      </p>


      <h3>No cookies, no tracking</h3>
      <p>
        This website sets no cookies, integrates no analytics or marketing tools and contains
        no forms. Beta contact runs via an ordinary email link that your mail program opens.
      </p>

      <h3>Fonts</h3>
      <p>
        All fonts used (Inter, Calistoga, JetBrains Mono) are delivered from this server. There
        is <strong>no connection to external font servers</strong> such as Google Fonts.
      </p>

      <h3>External links</h3>
      <p>
        This website links to external pages (e.g. GitHub). The respective provider is
        responsible for their data processing.
      </p>

      <h3>Encryption</h3>
      <p>
        This website is retrieved via a TLS-encrypted connection, recognisable by the
        “https://” in the address bar.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right at any time:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>to obtain access to your stored personal data (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
        <li>to request the rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
        <li>to request the erasure of your data (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
        <li>to request the restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
        <li>to request data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
        <li>
          to withdraw your consent to error reports and, in versions without an account, to the
          data donation at any time (Art. 7(3) GDPR), in the app
        </li>
        <li>
          to object to processing on the basis of legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR)
        </li>
        <li>to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Objection:</strong> Insofar as I process data on the basis of my legitimate
        interest (analysis, protection of invitations, preview of an invitation, details in the
        list of people, your shots remaining in a household that you have left and in copies,
        IP addresses in sign-in logs), you can object at any time on grounds relating to your
        particular situation, by email to <a href="mailto:hello@brewmind.app">hello@brewmind.app</a>. I then no longer process the data
        unless I can demonstrate compelling legitimate grounds. You can object to the analysis
        of your account data (Section&nbsp;4) without giving reasons, in the app or by email.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Erasure:</strong> You delete your account yourself in the app (Section&nbsp;4).
        What remains in the household in that case is set out there under “Deleting your
        account”. I delete shots of yours in a former household or in another person's copy at
        your request by email, as long as your account exists.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Access:</strong> Write to <a href="mailto:hello@brewmind.app">hello@brewmind.app</a> from the email address with which you
        signed in. I match your request to the account via this address. Which address is
        stored with your account is shown by the app under „Verwaltung“, „Konto“; if it differs
        from your own, please tell me what it is. If there is no address for your account, I
        cannot match it to a request; you then see your data in the app, and you can delete it
        there at any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Access in the household:</strong> If you are or were in a household with
        others, my response to your access request contains your own details, your shots (including those
        stored in a former household) and the shared beans and equipment of your household. It
        does not contain the shots and identifiers of the other people. If there are shots
        without a name in your household because the account behind them has been deleted, I
        tell you their number; you can see them in the app. As recipients I name to you the
        people who can see your shots today, in your household, in a former household and in
        the case of a copy taken along, with the name they have given themselves in the app.
      </p>
      <p>
        For requests about the earlier data donation and about error reports from versions
        without an account, please state your short ID (Section&nbsp;5). The competent
        supervisory authority is the Landesbeauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit
        Nordrhein-Westfalen (State Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information
        of North Rhine-Westphalia,
        <a href="https://www.ldi.nrw.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.ldi.nrw.de</a>).
      </p>

